menu "Claude Companion"

    config COMPANION_DEBUG_COMMANDS
        bool "Test-only serial console commands"
        default n
        help
            Adds console commands that exist only for testing on the bench. Some of
            them change state in ways a normal user never should:

              companion hostkey corrupt      overwrites the Host's host-key pin
              companion takeover | kick | hostcache set | watch test-fallback
              companion voice-upload-test
              wifi test drop
              power bench | sim | go | light test|raw | checkin hibernate
              power hib test|test-wake|probe|backstop <s> <n> | rail <n> on|off | imu suspend
              voice rec | test | test-bg | test-short | test-cancel
              ota read-test | update [corrupt-ram] | cancel | go-back | test-bootloop <1-3>

            The everyday commands (help, sshkey, companion status and the Host
            settings, sessions, logs, reply, wifi, ts, power status and settings,
            clock, ui, key, screenshot, reboot) are always built.

            Leave this off for a build you give to someone else. Turn it on in
            your local sdkconfig (idf.py menuconfig, or CONFIG_COMPANION_DEBUG_COMMANDS=y)
            for a development device.

    config COMPANION_OTA_TEST_NO_VALIDATE
        bool "Test build: never mark the image valid (rollback test)"
        default n
        depends on COMPANION_DEBUG_COMMANDS
        help
            Builds an image that never marks itself valid, for the rollback test. Never for a build you keep.

endmenu
